content.text:
The clean fix is:

- declare `foreman` in `Gemfile` under `group :development`;
- remove ad-hoc `gem install foreman` from the Dockerfile/runtime bootstrap;
- make `bin/dev` run `bundle exec foreman`.

That makes Foreman part of the application dependency graph and lockfile, so Docker volume initialization and Bundler agree about where the executable lives. I’ll patch that and update the lockfile.

