@@ -5,10 +5,10 @@
 The displayed basemap is basemap.at. The required attribution is therefore `Grundkarte: basemap.at`, with `basemap.at` linking to `https://basemap.at/`, following the Open Government Data Österreich CC-BY 4.0 naming guidance. These templates intentionally do not add OpenStreetMap attribution because no OSM basemap is displayed by these styles. If a future style adds another displayed source, that source must carry its own attribution without misleading users about the basemap.

 Both styles include:

-- the basemap.at vector source and layers, using the owned source id `basemap-at`, absolute `https://mapsneu.wien.gv.at/basemapv/bmapv/3857/tile/{z}/{y}/{x}.pbf` tile URLs instead of the upstream TileJSON's relative tile entries, and source `maxzoom: 15` so MapLibre overzooms from the highest reliable native basemap.at vector zoom;
-- a lower-opacity basemap.at `gelände` raster-shading layer controlled by `config/map_tiles.yml` (`terrain_opacity`, currently `0.35`) with source `maxzoom: 15` so it overzooms consistently with the vector basemap;
+- the basemap.at vector source and layers, using the owned source id `basemap-at`, absolute `https://mapsneu.wien.gv.at/basemapv/bmapv/3857/tile/{z}/{y}/{x}.pbf` tile URLs instead of the upstream TileJSON's relative tile entries, and upstream source `maxzoom: 19`; vector visibility/detail is controlled by the basemap.at-derived style layer `minzoom`/`maxzoom` ranges;
+- a lower-opacity basemap.at `gelände` raster-shading layer controlled by `config/map_tiles.yml` (`terrain_opacity`, currently `0.35`) with upstream source `maxzoom: 20`; the raster layer itself has no layer-level zoom range;
 - one Austrian Rocks vector source named `austrian-rocks` using a development-safe PMTiles URL in the committed template;
 - style layers for every source layer in `MapTiles::LayerContract.layer_names`.

 During publication, `MapTiles::StyleMaterializer` writes immutable versioned light/dark style JSON artifacts and rewrites the `austrian-rocks` source URL to the exact versioned PMTiles URL for that release. Clients should fetch the non-cached release manifest, then load the versioned style URL from `styles.light` or `styles.dark`.

