 The displayed basemap is basemap.at. The required attribution is therefore `Grundkarte: basemap.at`, with `basemap.at` linking to `https://basemap.at/`, following the Open Government Data Österreich CC-BY 4.0 naming guidance. These templates intentionally do not add OpenStreetMap attribution because no OSM basemap is displayed by these styles. If a future style adds another displayed source, that source must carry its own attribution without misleading users about the basemap.

 Both styles include:

-- the Bergwerk basemap.at vector source and layers, normalized to the owned source id `basemap-at`, using Bergwerk-provided `https://basemap.bergwerk-gis.at/basemap-download/webapp/api/tiles/basemap-at-vector/{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf` tile URLs and source/layer zoom metadata as provided by that style;
+- the Bergwerk basemap.at vector source and layers, normalized to the owned source id `basemap-at`, using CORS-enabled `https://basemap.bergwerk-gis.at/api/tiles/basemap-at-vector/{z}/{x}/{y}.pbf` tile URLs and Bergwerk source/layer zoom metadata as provided by that style;
 - a lower-opacity basemap.at `gelände` raster-shading layer controlled by `config/map_tiles.yml` (`terrain_opacity`, currently `0.35`), normalized to source id `basemap-at-gelaende`, using the Bergwerk style's terrain raster source metadata as provided;
 - one Austrian Rocks vector source named `austrian-rocks` using a development-safe PMTiles URL in the committed template;
 - style layers for every source layer in `MapTiles::LayerContract.layer_names`.

